## 12. Rule-Based Red-Flag Layer

Defined in `backend/app/pipeline/rules.py`. This is a flat list of compiled regex patterns that run against every clause. It is:

- **Deterministic:** Same input always produces the same flags.
- **Auditable:** Every flag has a `rule_name` and `matched_text`.
- **Independent of the LLM:** Works even if Gemini is down or rate-limited.
- **A safety net:** Catches patterns that embedding similarity might miss.

The patterns are defined in Section 7 Stage 3a above. They are loaded from a config dict (not hardcoded in the regex calls) so they can be extended without modifying pipeline logic.

