## 15. Frontend ↔ Backend Integration Changes

### What Changes

| Current State | Target State |
|---------------|-------------|
| `mockData.ts` defines `Document` and `Clause` types manually | Types auto-generated from OpenAPI into `src/api/types.ts` |
| `processUploadedFile()` fakes a timer and returns hardcoded data | Calls `POST /api/documents` with the actual file, then polls `GET /api/documents/{id}` |
| Demo docs loaded from hardcoded `mockDocuments` array | Demo docs fetched from `GET /api/demo-documents` (pre-analyzed, cached on backend) |
| Risk levels are `"low"` / `"medium"` / `"high"` | Risk levels are `"standard"` / `"cautionary"` / `"risky"` — update helper functions |
| No error states | Handle `status: "error"` responses, show user-friendly error messages |

### New Frontend Files

1. **`src/api/types.ts`** — Auto-generated by `openapi-typescript`. Never edit.
2. **`src/api/client.ts`** — Fetch wrapper:
   ```typescript
   const API_BASE = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL || 'http://localhost:8000';

   export async function uploadDocument(file: File): Promise<{ id: string }> { ... }
   export async function uploadText(text: string): Promise<{ id: string }> { ... }
   export async function getDocument(id: string): Promise<DocumentAnalysisResult> { ... }
   export async function getDemoDocuments(): Promise<DocumentAnalysisResult[]> { ... }
   ```
3. **`src/hooks/useDocumentAnalysis.ts`** — Custom hook that manages upload → poll → result lifecycle with loading/error states.

### Polling Strategy

```typescript
// Poll every 2 seconds until status !== "processing"
const poll = async (docId: string) => {
  const result = await getDocument(docId);
  if (result.status === 'processing') {
    setTimeout(() => poll(docId), 2000);
  } else {
    setDocument(result);
  }
};
```

